# [DD-13b.W23.3] `under`'s KEY TUPLE IS FOUR COMPONENTS, and this file is
# the regression for a bug that shipped between two commits of one step.
#
# §2.17: two `under` lines for one (convention, subject, kind, startpos)
# are REFUSED as a duplicate, not last-wins. The tuple ranges over fields
# INSIDE the `qualified-line` value, so extracting it is parser code —
# the ONE named exception §2.25.3 records — which is exactly the kind of
# rule a schema cannot check on its owner's behalf.
#
# THE BUG: the extractor read the convention with `strchr(v, ':')`, on a
# spelling that has no colon (`under <convention> <case-line>`, SPACE-
# separated — leg B's arm has no colon and leg C REFUSES the colon form
# by name). With no colon the convention came out EMPTY and every later
# component slid one place left, so two lines differing only in SUBJECT
# or only in STARTPOS were refused as duplicates while the REFUSING
# fixture still went red for an unrelated reason. A refuse-only pair
# cannot see that: it passes for the wrong reason.
#
# So the four lines below differ in ONE component each, and all four must
# be ACCEPTED. `under_key_duplicate.rxtin` is the refusing half.
pattern a|ab
under pcre2 m "ab" 0 1
under pcre2 m "cd" 0 1
under pcre2 m 1 "ab" 1 2
under pcre2 n "zz"
under posix m "ab" 0 2
m "ab" 0 1
